//! The C ABI of the `ZhuyinType` engine (`include/zhuyin.h`, generated by cbindgen and checked in).
//!
//! Handles are opaque: [`ZtEngine`] (the lexicon, language models and personal data), [`ZtComposer`] (one
//! composition state machine), [`ZtReranker`] and [`ZtSyllableScorer`] (the neural models' decisions in Rust, with
//! the numeric inference supplied by the host as C callbacks, so the macOS app keeps Core ML in Swift).
//!
//! # Ownership
//! - Strings passed in are UTF-8, NUL-terminated and borrowed for the call.  Strings returned (`char *`) belong to
//!   the caller and are freed with [`zt_string_free`]; lists and presentations with their own `_free` functions.
//! - Handles are created by `zt_*_new`/`zt_*_open` and freed by the matching `zt_*_free`.  A composer keeps its engine
//!   alive; freeing the engine handle first is allowed.
//! - Callback contexts: the `release` function of a hook or model (when not NULL) is called exactly once, when the
//!   hook is replaced or its owner is freed.
//!
//! # Threading
//! - An engine may be used from any thread, also concurrently.  A composer is used by one thread at a time (it may
//!   move between threads).  Rerankers and syllable scorers may be shared between threads; their model calls are
//!   serialized.
//! - Callbacks run synchronously on the thread that made the call into the library, and must not call back into the
//!   composer that invoked them.  Views passed to callbacks (`ZtSentences`, `ZtStrings`, `ZtCandidateRows`) are valid
//!   only until the callback returns.
//!
//! # Errors
//! Functions that can fail return NULL, `false` or −1 and, when `error` is not NULL, store a message there (free it
//! with [`zt_string_free`]).
// The whole crate is the C boundary: raw pointers from the host are dereferenced after the documented checks.
#![allow(unsafe_code)]

mod composer;
mod engine;
mod models;
mod strings;

pub use composer::*;
pub use engine::*;
pub use models::*;
pub use strings::*;
